	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg14229"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=179" title="View the profile of Kelce">Kelce</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 129<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/megatron.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Asshole.<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kelce@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kelce@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=179"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.shadowsanddust.org" title="Linkz" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:haplessrogue@gmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1402.msg14229#msg14229"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1402.msg14229#msg14229">Re: WoW guild dynamics</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> February 03, 2005, 10:39:11 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Not at all what I described. Battlegrounds is primarily PvP with sidequests to eliminate the opposition. Noninstanced raid content is what I was wishing for; which allows for competition, not elimination.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg14263"></a><a name="new"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=393" title="View the profile of Zerxes">Zerxes</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 82<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=393"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1402.msg14263#msg14263"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1402.msg14263#msg14263">Re: WoW guild dynamics</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #3 on:</b> February 04, 2005, 06:41:14 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1402.msg14229#msg14229">Quote from: Kelce on February 03, 2005, 10:39:11 pm</a></div><div class="quote">Not at all what I described. Battlegrounds is primarily PvP with sidequests to eliminate the opposition. Noninstanced raid content is what I was wishing for; which allows for competition, not elimination.<br /></div><br />Taken straight from the FAQ of Sigil&#039;s Vanguard: Saga of Heroes:<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">A degree of competition for resources is good in an otherwise primarily PvE (Player vs. Environment) game. There should still be an incentive to have a sense of urgency and to reach certain areas before others, etc. Certainly, were everyone guaranteed equal access to all content, the players&#039; sense of accomplishment would be virtually eliminated.<br /><br />That said, it can go too far. By having a large world, plenty of content, and an advanced encounter system, we hope to avoid &#039;too much&#039; competition.</div><br />Looks like this is the game for you and those folks who actually enjoy &quot;racing&quot; other guilds for content.&nbsp; My interpretation of that quote is this:&nbsp; We won&#039;t use instancing (that&#039;s pretty much a verified fact taken from Brad McQuaid himself), so there will be &quot;racing&quot; for mobs between guilds, but there won&#039;t be &quot;cockblocking&quot; because there will be plenty of content (i.e., we won&#039;t have an Emperor --- Vex Thall bottleneck on progression).&nbsp; <br /><br />I&#039;m not sure I have a problem with that provided the other content is equally desirable.&nbsp; Problem is, I don&#039;t see how they can do that and create an incentive to &quot;race&quot; other guilds.&nbsp; After all, if mob [a] spawns and my guild goes &quot;ooooooh, everyone run to zone <li type="square"> real quick to kill mob[a]&quot; but then we find out that mob [b] is up, who has equally good loot and the time and difficulty in getting to and killing the mob are equal, and we find another guild is racing to mob[a], why would we even bother racing?&nbsp; Just go and kill mob[b].&nbsp; To use EQ, if the difference between the content available is a full pop in Plane of Fire and a full pop in Plane of Air, that isn&#039;t &quot;equal&quot; content and people will always want to farm Plane of Fire, and the loser will always get Plane of Air.<br /><br />My personal prediction:&nbsp; SoH will never top 300K subscribers.&nbsp; Its niche in the MMORPG market will be the &quot;hardcore&quot; raiders, who will soon find out they make a very, very small minority of MMORPG players.<br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
